{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_df9651c9e47348b8afd4b6f4","name":"read","arguments":{"limit":150,"offset":1,"path":"src/routing.rs"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_870b61bcd0fb4225abeee846","name":"read","arguments":{"limit":150,"offset":1,"path":"src/report.rs"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":858,"output":49,"cacheRead":11008,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1,"totalTokens":11915,"cost":{"input":0.00012869999999999998,"output":0.0000245,"cacheRead":0.00033024,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00048343999999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792429806182,"responseId":"gen-1792429806-26RWAAYK1QVeg2QQ3nrR","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_df9651c9e47348b8afd4b6f4","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"//! Purpose: Dry-run fault routing — proposals for tool-fault tickets in\n//! the faulting tool's repository (openspec add-fault-ticket-routing).\n//! Responsibilities: filter tier-2 report rows to tool faults (failing\n//! checks without an `ERR_*` code), tally DISTINCT models per fault key\n//! (scenario, fault-class, tool) using the same threshold semantics as\n//! report.rs (min(3, |configured model registry|)), key the target\n//! repository on the scenario definition's recorded tool (never the\n//! report row's tool field, which is hardcoded for live trials), and\n//! emit proposal rows with the fingerprint token\n//! `evallerina:<scenario>:<fault-class>` and the full machine-checkable\n//! schema. Phase 1 is dry-run only: every emitted decision is `dry_run`\n//! (mapped tool) or `skipped`/`unmapped_tool` — no `bd` invocations\n//! happen in the dry-run path. Phase 2 (evallerina-2bz) adds the filing\n//! path behind explicit authorization: fingerprint-token dedup in the\n//! target repo (`--status open` always pinned — closed issues must not\n//! block re-filing a regressed fault), then `bd create` in the target\n//! repo cwd with exit-code + id capture, then the tracked-export\n//! invariant (`bd export -o .beads/issues.jsonl`). Every bd invocation\n//! is routed through `run_bd` (cwd-scoped subprocess) and is injectable\n//! so tests can spy on calls; `bd` failure is `skipped`/`bd_failure`,\n//! never fatal — filing is an optimization over the report.\n//! Rationale: the fault taxonomy routes tool faults to tickets in the\n//! tool's repo, but the value that made evallerina useful (evallerina-2rr,\n//! -00n, -54f) all required hand-filing from dashboard findings. Routing\n//! makes that mechanical, with a dry-run default so cross-repo writes\n//! stay behind an explicit local opt-in, and loud errors on unknown\n//! scenarios (mirroring report.rs: never a silent bucket).\n\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\n\n/// The cross-model routing threshold — identical semantics to\n/// report.rs: a fault key observed in trial rows from at least this\n/// many distinct models (3, or the full configured registry when\n/// smaller) is routed.\nconst ROUTING_THRESHOLD: usize = 3;\n\n/// One dry-run proposal row (the proposed-tickets.jsonl schema, design\n/// §6): machine-checkable so the CI artifact is reviewable without\n/// reading code.\n#[derive(Debug, PartialEq)]\npub struct ProposalRow {\n    /// The scenario definition's recorded tool — the repo key.\n    pub tool: String,\n    /// Mapped repository path (null until/unless the tool is mapped).\n    pub repo: Option<String>,\n    pub scenario: String,\n    pub fault_class: String,\n    /// Fingerprint token: `evallerina:<scenario>:<fault-class>`.\n    pub token: String,\n    /// `dry_run` (mapped, not filed) or `skipped` (unmapped tool).\n    pub decision: String,\n    /// Null unless skipped (`unmapped_tool`).\n    pub reason: Option<String>,\n    /// Null in dry-run; set only when a ticket is filed (Phase 2).\n    pub bd_issue_id: Option<String>,\n    /// Provenance of the contributing trial rows (deduped by model):\n    /// report row scenario/model/tool values.\n    pub row_provenance: Vec<ProvenanceRow>,\n}\n\n/// One contributing trial row's provenance.\n#[derive(Debug, PartialEq)]\npub struct ProvenanceRow {\n    pub scenario: String,\n    pub model: String,\n    /// The report row's tool value — provenance only, never the repo key.\n    pub tool: String,\n}\n\nimpl ProposalRow {\n    /// Serialize to the proposed-tickets.jsonl JSON object.\n    pub fn to_json(&self) -> serde_json::Value {\n        serde_json::json!({\n            \"tool\": self.tool,\n            \"repo\": self.repo,\n            \"scenario\": self.scenario,\n            \"fault_class\": self.fault_class,\n            \"token\": self.token,\n            \"decision\": self.decision,\n            \"reason\": self.reason,\n            \"bd_issue_id\": self.bd_issue_id,\n            \"row_provenance\": self.row_provenance.iter()\n                .map(|p| serde_json::json!({\n                    \"scenario\": p.scenario,\n                    \"model\": p.model,\n                    \"tool\": p.tool,\n                }))\n                .collect::<Vec<_>>(),\n        })\n    }\n}\n\n/// Propose dry-run tickets from tier-2 report rows.\n///\n/// `rows` are parsed report rows (same inputs as report.rs: tier-2\n/// trial events, tier-1 rows without model attribution, absent records).\n/// `configured_models` is the model registry the rotation was configured\n/// with — it defines the routing threshold (min(3, registry size));\n/// empty is a loud error, no routing threshold exists. `scenario_tool_of`\n/// resolves a scenario to the tool its *definition* recorded (proposals\n/// key the repo on this, never on the row's tool field); an unknown\n/// scenario is a loud error. `repo_map` maps tool name → repo path (the\n/// parsed routing.toml); a mapped-but-unregistered tool surfaces as\n/// `skipped`/`unmapped_tool`, never a silent drop.\npub fn propose(\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\n    configured_models: &[String],\n    scenario_tool_of: &dyn Fn(&str) -> Option<String>,\n    repo_map: &BTreeMap<String, String>,\n) -> Result<Vec<ProposalRow>, String> {\n    if configured_models.is_empty() {\n        return Err(\"configured model registry is empty — no routing threshold exists\".into());\n    }\n    let routing_threshold = configured_models.len().min(ROUTING_THRESHOLD);\n\n    // Fault key (scenario, fault-class, tool-from-scenario) →\n    // distinct models + occurrences + provenance rows.\n    let mut faults: BTreeMap<FaultKey, FaultTally> = BTreeMap::new();\n\n    for row in rows {\n        let kind = row.get(\"kind\").and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str);\n        if kind == Some(\"absent\") {\n            // Absent cells are the record that a cell did not run;\n            // never failures, never dropped (anti-goal — mirrored\n            // from report.rs).\n            continue;\n        }\n        let scenario = row\n            .get(\"scenario\")\n            .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str)\n            .ok_or(\"report row lacks a `scenario` field\")?;\n        let row_tool = row\n            .get(\"tool\")\n            .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str)\n            .ok_or(\"report row lacks a `tool` field\")?;\n        let report_version = row\n            .get(\"report_version\")\n            .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_u64)\n            .ok_or(\"report row lacks a `report_version` field\")?;\n        if report_version != 1 {\n            return Err(format!(\n                \"report row carries report_version {report_version}; routing aggregates version 1 only\"\n            ));\n        }\n        // The repo keys on the scenario definition's recorded tool,\n        // not the row's tool field (hardcoded in live rows; the hhs\n        // bug showed attribution drifts). Unknown scenario → loud.\n        let recorded_tool = scenario_tool_of(scenario).ok_or_else(|| {\n            format!(\"scenario '{scenario}' has no recorded tool — refusing to route\")\n        })?;\n\n[285 more lines in file. Use offset=151 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792429810715},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_870b61bcd0fb4225abeee846","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"//! Purpose: Tier-1/2 report aggregation into the per-channel fault\n//! dashboard (evallerina-48g).\n//! Responsibilities: aggregate report_version 1 rows (tier-2 rotation\n//! events and tier-1 rows without model attribution) into a\n//! per-output-channel × check-code × model-id fault matrix, apply the\n//! evals-guidelines fault routing (tool faults → tool tickets; agent\n//! faults → AIX-channel work only at the cross-model threshold),\n//! surface absent, rate_limited, and http_error cells as coverage\n//! records — never failures, never dropped — and refuse loudly on unmappable scenarios\n//! instead of silently bucketing them.\n//! Rationale: evals-guidelines \"Fault routing\" and \"suite-wide\n//! aggregation\" requirements. The dashboard deliberately carries no\n//! single aggregate score: per-capability breakdown is a hard\n//! requirement, and a collapse into one number hides exactly the\n//! channel × code × model signal the routing rule needs.\n\nuse serde_json::json;\nuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};\n\n/// Version of the dashboard shape. Additive evolution only within a\n/// version; breaking changes bump this.\npub const DASHBOARD_VERSION: u32 = 1;\n\n/// The evals-guidelines cross-model routing threshold for agent faults\n/// within one output channel.\nconst ROUTING_THRESHOLD: usize = 3;\n\n/// The output channel a live scenario's checks probe (the fault-routing\n/// key per evals-guidelines: suggestions, envelope, managed-block, or\n/// artifact surface). Registered for every live scenario; the channel\n/// must exist before rotation day, not after the first dashboard run.\npub fn scenario_channel(name: &str) -> Option<&'static str> {\n    match name {\n        \"wai-hint-adherence-smoke\"\n        | \"wai-hint-adherence-corrupt-config\"\n        | \"dont-hint-adherence-lifecycle\" => Some(\"envelope\"),\n        \"wai-hint-adherence-typo\" => Some(\"suggestions\"),\n        \"wai-doc-drift-stale-agents-md\" | \"dont-doc-drift-stale-lifecycle\" => Some(\"artifact\"),\n        _ => None,\n    }\n}\n\n/// One accumulator key in the routing maps: agent faults key on\n/// (channel, code), tool faults on (tool, check, channel) because they\n/// carry no code by contract.\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord)]\nenum FaultKey {\n    /// Agent fault: the `ERR_*` taxonomy code within one output channel.\n    Agent { channel: String, code: String },\n    /// Tool fault: no code; routed to the tool's repository.\n    Tool {\n        tool: String,\n        check: String,\n        channel: String,\n    },\n}\n\n/// Accumulated occurrences for one fault key: total count plus the set\n/// of distinct model ids observed (empty for non-tier-2 rows).\n#[derive(Debug, Default)]\nstruct FaultTally {\n    occurrences: usize,\n    models: BTreeSet<String>,\n    scenarios: BTreeSet<String>,\n}\n\n/// Aggregate report_version 1 rows into the dashboard JSON.\n///\n/// `rows` are parsed report rows as [`serde_json::Value`]: tier-2\n/// rotation events (`kind: trial | absent`) or tier-1 rows without a\n/// `model` field (grouped as non-tier-2 per the report contract).\n/// `configured_models` is the model registry the rotation was\n/// configured with — it defines the routing threshold (3, or the full\n/// registry size when fewer than three are configured). `channel_of`\n/// resolves a scenario to the output channel its checks probe; an\n/// unknown scenario is a loud error, never a silent bucket.\n///\n/// The returned value is the serialized dashboard shape: no single\n/// aggregate score, per-capability breakdown only.\npub fn aggregate_rows(\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\n    configured_models: &[String],\n    channel_of: &dyn Fn(&str) -> Option<&'static str>,\n) -> Result<serde_json::Value, String> {\n    if configured_models.is_empty() {\n        return Err(\"configured model registry is empty — no routing threshold exists\".into());\n    }\n    let routing_threshold = configured_models.len().min(ROUTING_THRESHOLD);\n\n    let mut matrix_cells: BTreeMap<(String, String, String), FaultTally> = BTreeMap::new();\n    let mut routings: BTreeMap<FaultKey, FaultTally> = BTreeMap::new();\n    let mut coverage = Coverage::default();\n    let mut report_versions = BTreeSet::new();\n\n    for row in rows {\n        let kind = row.get(\"kind\").and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str);\n        if kind == Some(\"absent\") {\n            // Absent cells are the record that a cell did not run; they\n            // are never failures and never dropped (anti-goal).\n            coverage.absent += 1;\n            continue;\n        }\n        let status = row\n            .get(\"status\")\n            .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str)\n            .ok_or(\"report row lacks a `status` field\")?;\n        let scenario = row\n            .get(\"scenario\")\n            .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str)\n            .ok_or(\"report row lacks a `scenario` field\")?;\n        let tool = row\n            .get(\"tool\")\n            .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str)\n            .ok_or(\"report row lacks a `tool` field\")?;\n        let checks = row\n            .get(\"checks\")\n            .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_array)\n            .ok_or(\"report row lacks a `checks` array\")?;\n        let report_version = row\n            .get(\"report_version\")\n            .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_u64)\n            .ok_or(\"report row lacks a `report_version` field\")?;\n        if report_version != 1 {\n            return Err(format!(\n                \"report row carries report_version {report_version}; this dashboard aggregates version 1 only\"\n            ));\n        }\n        report_versions.insert(report_version);\n\n        let channel = channel_of(scenario).ok_or_else(|| {\n            format!(\"scenario '{scenario}' has no declared output channel — refusing to aggregate\")\n        })?;\n\n        let model = row.get(\"model\").and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str);\n        match model {\n            Some(_) => {\n                coverage.trials += 1;\n                bump_status(&mut coverage, status)?;\n            }\n            None => coverage.non_tier2 += 1,\n        }\n\n        for check in checks {\n            let name = check\n                .get(\"name\")\n                .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str)\n                .ok_or(\"check row lacks a `name` field\")?;\n            let passed = check\n                .get(\"passed\")\n                .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_bool)\n\n[210 more lines in file. Use offset=151 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792429810715}]}
