{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me look at the workflow file and check tests/routing.rs to understand existing routing tests, and check what scenario_tool_of looks like — how does the scenario definition record a tool? Let me check src/scenario.rs.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Now let me look at the workflow file and check tests/routing.rs to understand existing routing tests, and check what scenario_tool_of looks like — how does the scenario definition record a tool? Let me check src/scenario.rs.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-266ca1db-4924-4f46-8e47-653b924e0fec","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".github/workflows/evals-rotation.yml","offset":1,"limit":80}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-b2b8490b-6fe5-4ee2-87b4-cda432602757","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"tool\" src/scenario.rs | head -20; echo ---; grep -n \"propose\\|scenario_tool_of\\|recorded_tool\" tests/routing.rs | head -30","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":24794,"output":134,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":46,"totalTokens":24928,"cost":{"input":0.0037191,"output":0.000067,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0037860999999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792429827354,"responseId":"gen-1792429827-nsTnMPjkRApwBB7WnmsJ","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-266ca1db-4924-4f46-8e47-653b924e0fec","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Tier-2 scheduled rotation (scenario × model cells).\n#\n# Split out of evallerina-5ap (the rotation workflow is evallerina-aay).\n# The live runner it invokes landed with evallerina-1vw (src/live.rs —\n# OpenRouter :free action protocol); this workflow iterates the ordered\n# model registry (:free ids first) × the live scenario battery and\n# prints one JSON event per cell: a report_version 1 trial row, or an\n# absent record when the per-run wall-clock budget skipped the cell.\n# Live runs NEVER gate a push (schedule + manual dispatch only).\n#\n# Budget rules per evals-ci.md: :free ids first, marginal cost ~zero USD;\n# a per-run wall-clock budget applies (--budget-mins) — cells skipped\n# past the window are recorded as absent, not failed. 429 semantics\n# (one >=2s retry, then rate_limited, never silent model substitution)\n# live in the runner. Requires the OPENROUTER_API_KEY repo secret;\n# without it the run fails loudly (no silent degradation).\n\nname: evals-rotation\n\non:\n  workflow_dispatch: {}\n  # Weekly rotation (7-day cycle, within the <=14-day budget): Monday\n  # 04:00 UTC — after the tier-1 replay window (0 3 * * *).\n  schedule:\n    - cron: \"0 4 * * 1\"\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: evals-rotation\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\nenv:\n  CARGO_TERM_COLOR: always\n  RUST_BACKTRACE: 1\n\njobs:\n  rotation:\n    name: Tier 2 — live rotation (scenario × model cells)\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    # Job ceiling 30 min vs --budget-mins 20: the slack lets the runner\n    # finish the trial in flight and record every skipped cell absent.\n    timeout-minutes: 30\n\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable\n\n      - uses: Swatinem/rust-cache@v2\n\n      # The eval targets themselves, pinned to released tags: the\n      # trials execute the tools, so the runner needs them on PATH.\n      - name: Install eval targets (wai, dont)\n        run: |\n          cargo install --locked --git https://github.com/charly-vibes/wai --tag v2026.10.9\n          cargo install --locked --git https://github.com/charly-vibes/dont --tag v0.4.0\n\n      - name: Run tier-2 rotation\n        env:\n          OPENROUTER_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.OPENROUTER_API_KEY }}\n        run: |\n          mkdir -p reports\n          cargo run --release -- live --budget-mins 20 \\\n            | tee -a reports/tier2-rotation.jsonl\n\n      - name: Upload rotation rows\n        if: always()\n        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\n        with:\n          name: tier2-rotation\n          path: reports/tier2-rotation.jsonl\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792429845605},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-b2b8490b-6fe5-4ee2-87b4-cda432602757","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"47:/// - `status-error-envelope-carries-remediation-hint` (tool fault if broken)\n51:/// - `init-recovery-ok` (tool fault if broken)\n108:/// - `typo-stderr-carries-did-you-mean` (tool fault if the DidYouMean\n109:///   hint is absent from stderr — the channel is the tool's promise)\n113:/// - `init-recovery-ok` (tool fault if broken)\n142:/// - `config-error-envelope-carries-remediation-hint` (tool fault)\n146:/// - `status-recovery-ok` (tool fault if broken)\n178:///    retries with a `file://` URI which the tool itself rejects\n190:/// - `trust-error-carries-reason-remediation` (tool fault)\n193:/// - `flag-error-carries-evidence-remediation` (tool fault)\n196:/// - `file-uri-rejected-with-repair-hint` (tool fault)\n200:/// - `show-reports-verified` (tool fault if the state machine did not\n292:/// - `init-recovery-ok` (tool fault if broken)\n329:/// - `show-reports-verified` (tool fault if the state machine did not\n371:/// - `gate-exit-blocks` (tool fault if the gate stops blocking)\n372:/// - `gate-envelope-names-seam` (tool fault if the finding is gone)\n374:/// - `guidance-reports-same-seam` (tool fault if guidance disagrees with\n430:/// - `status-error-envelope-carries-remediation-hint` (tool fault)\n433:/// - `init-recovery-ok` (tool fault if broken)\n---\n7://! proposed-tickets.jsonl row schema.\n176:    let proposals = routing::propose(&rows, &three_models(), &recorded_wai, &repo_map())\n195:    let proposals = routing::propose(&rows, &three_models(), &recorded_wai, &repo_map())\n216:    let proposals = routing::propose(&rows, &three_models(), &recorded_wai, &repo_map())\n232:    let proposals = routing::propose(&rows, &three_models(), &recorded_wai, &empty_map)\n242:fn repo_keys_on_recorded_tool_not_row_tool() {\n256:    let proposals = routing::propose(&rows, &three_models(), &recorded_dont, &drifted_map)\n321:        routing::propose(&rows, &three_models(), &two_scenarios, &map).expect(\"routing succeeds\");\n546:    let err = routing::propose(&rows, &three_models(), &recorded_wai, &repo_map())\n557:    let proposals = routing::propose(&rows, &three_models(), &recorded_wai, &repo_map())\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792429845605}]}
