{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":6563,"output":2070,"cacheRead":26880,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":2016,"totalTokens":35513,"cost":{"input":0.00098445,"output":0.001035,"cacheRead":0.0008064,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00282585}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now let me check lib.rs exports and tests/routing.rs top (trial_row helper) plus how the CLI-level test might work. Also check `main.rs` uses only lib exports; integration test uses `evallerina::routing`.\n\nPlan the red/green sequence:\n\n**Step 1 (RED):** test in tests/report_aggregation.rs: `--file` without `--route` is an error → `report::validate_route_flags(false, true).is_err()` and `Ok(())` for (true,true), (true,false), (false,false). Run → fails (function doesn't exist). GREEN: add validate_route_flags to report.rs + wire into main.rs (--file requires --route). Commit.\n\n**Step 2 (RED):** test: report --route dry-run on fabricated rows → routed summary present, dry_run > 0, report_version 1, proposals written... writing jsonl is main.rs side; the library test can test `attach_routing` returns proposals and mutates dashboard. For \"proposed-tickets.jsonl written\" — that's CLI behavior. Can integration tests cover it? They could invoke the binary via CARGO_BIN_EXE (env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_evallerina\")). That's a good approach: integration test can run the actual binary with a temp rows file. That tests end-to-end: routed field present, jsonl written. That's heavier but faithful to the brief. Let's do both: unit-ish tests of attach_routing + one bin test using CARGO_BIN_EXE_evallerina for the CLI surface (jsonl written).\n\nWait — does bin need cargo test to build? Integration tests can use env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_evallerina\") which builds the bin automatically. Good.\n\n**Step 3 (RED):** report without --route → no routed field, no jsonl. Bin test: run binary without --route on rows file, output JSON has no \"routed\", no jsonl file.\n\n**Step 4 (RED):** routing failures: unmapped tool → skipped counted, report succeeds. Test: attach_routing with empty repo_map → Ok, summary skipped > 0. Also bin-level: --route with rows → exit 0.\n\n**Step 5:** workflow edit.\n\nDesign report.rs API:\n\n```rust\npub fn validate_route_flags(route: bool, file: bool) -> Result<(), String>\n\npub fn scenario_tool_of(name: &str) -> Option<String>\n\n/// Attach the additive `routed` summary to the dashboard after running\n/// the routing step. Returns the proposals (for jsonl serialization).\npub fn attach_routing(\n    dashboard: &mut serde_json::Value,\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\n    configured_models: &[String],\n    repo_map: &BTreeMap<String, String>,\n    file_authorized: bool,\n    run_bd: &mut routing::BdRunner,\n) -> Result<Vec<routing::ProposalRow>, String>\n```\n\nmain.rs run_report:\n\n```rust\nfn run_report(path: &str, route: bool, file: bool) -> Result<ExitCode, String> {\n    evallerina::report::validate_route_flags(route, file)?;\n    ... rows ...\n    let mut dashboard = aggregate_rows(...)?;\n    let mut proposals = Vec::new();\n    if route {\n        let routing_toml = std::fs::read_to_string(\"routing.toml\").map_err(...)?;  // relative to cwd? better: resolve relative to manifest? CLI run from repo root typically. Use env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")? For release binary that's compile-time path — fine since it's a repo tool. Actually routing.toml lives at repo root; discover_root gives repo root via git. Use routing::discover_root() + join. Hmm simpler: read \"routing.toml\" relative to cwd — but workflows run from repo root. Tests run bin in temp dirs though (CWD of test = crate root? cargo runs integration tests with cwd = package root). Bin tests spawn with .current_dir(tempdir) → routing.toml wouldn't be found... unless test spawns bin with current_dir = crate root or passes an env. Hmm.\n\nOptions: run_bin test spawns with current_dir(temp) and needs routing.toml. I could copy routing.toml into the temp dir? But binary reads \"routing.toml\" from cwd. If main resolves via discover_root() (git rev-parse), temp dir isn't a git repo → error. \n\nSimplest robust: main reads `routing.toml` from the current directory, falling back to CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR. In the bin test, spawn the binary with current_dir = temp dir, and first copy routing.toml from CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR into temp. That's hermetic. OK.\n```\n\nActually also `resolve_repo` resolves relative repo paths against evallerina root — in dry-run, proposals just carry repo path strings; no resolution needed in dry-run? propose() just takes repo_map values as-is. to_jsonl includes repo path. Fine.\n\nFor `--file` path (not in tests, but wired): file_proposals needs repos to exist; main passes routing::run_bd as runner. Fine.\n\nWriting jsonl: next to report path → parent dir of path: `Path::new(path).parent()` — if empty use \".\". \n\nMain flow:\n\n```rust\nif route {\n    let root = ...; // for nothing? propose doesn't need root\n    let content = read routing.toml (cwd, fallback manifest dir)\n    let repo_map = evallerina::routing::parse_routing_toml(&content)?;\n    let mut run = evallerina::routing::run_bd;\n    let proposals = evallerina::report::attach_routing(&mut dashboard, &rows, &configured, &repo_map, file, &mut run)?;\n    let jsonl = evallerina::routing::to_jsonl(&proposals);\n    let out_path = report_path.parent().unwrap_or(Path::new(\".\")).join(\"proposed-tickets.jsonl\");\n    std::fs::write(&out_path, jsonl).map_err(...)?;\n}\n```\n\nWhere should the routing.toml reading + writing jsonl live — main.rs per brief (\"write proposed-tickets.jsonl next to the report when routing ran\" listed under src/report.rs responsibilities... Brief says report.rs: \"call routing::propose after aggregation when --route; attach routed summary to the report JSON; write proposed-tickets.jsonl next to the report when routing ran\". So report.rs should do the writing too. So put a higher-level function in report.rs:\n\n```rust\npub fn route_report(\n    dashboard: &mut serde_json::Value,\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\n    configured_models: &[String],\n    report_path: &Path,\n    file_authorized: bool,\n    run_bd: &mut BdRunner,\n) -> Result<Vec<ProposalRow>, String>\n```\n\nThis parses routing.toml (path resolution: current dir then manifest dir), attaches summary, writes jsonl. But library code writing files... acceptable given brief. But routing.toml location from library: use std::env::current_dir, fallback env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\"). Library binary tests spawn bin in temp cwd with a copied routing.toml → works. Integration tests calling route_report directly would read routing.toml from crate root cwd (cargo test cwd = package root) → routing.toml present → works, but tests then write jsonl into... report_path parent — tests pass a temp path. OK.\n\nHmm, but tests calling attach_routing directly avoid fs. I'll split:\n\n- `attach_routing(dashboard, rows, configured, repo_map, file_authorized, run_bd) -> Result<Vec<ProposalRow>, String>` — pure computation.\n- `run_routing_step(dashboard, rows, configured, report_path, file_authorized, run_bd) -> Result<Vec<ProposalRow>, String>` — loads routing.toml, calls attach_routing, writes jsonl. Used by main; bin test covers it.\n\nLet me now also think about `filed`/`existing` counts in dry-run: zero. Summary json:\n\n```json\n{\"filed\": 0, \"existing\": 0, \"dry_run\": 2, \"skipped\": 1}\n```\n\nTest 2 asserts dry_run > 0 and dashboard[\"report_version\"] == 1.\n\nTest 4: rows with a tool-fault scenario mapped but repo_map lacking the tool → skipped. In dry-run propose: unmapped tool → decision skipped, reason unmapped_tool. Summary skipped count = number of proposal rows skipped. Note proposals only exist above threshold. So fabricate 3 models × tool fault, repo_map without \"wai\" → one skipped proposal.\n\nTest \"absent rows never routed\": rows containing only absent kind → proposals empty, routed summary all zeros; assert dry_run==0, skipped==0, proposals.is_empty(). Note: absent rows lack tool/checks etc — aggregate_rows handles kind absent by counting coverage; propose also skips them. But rows array passed to propose — the absent row has no \"scenario\" field... in my test I'll include scenario in the absent row (the real absent record has scenario, model, repetition). propose skips before touching scenario. Good.\n\nAlso dashboard report_version: aggregate_rows sets report_version from rows; with absent-only rows... report_versions set is empty → defaults to 1. Good.\n\nBut careful: absent-only rows into aggregate_rows — coverage.absent incremented; fine.\n\nNow the bin tests. Use std::process::Command with env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_evallerina\"). Check the bin name in Cargo.toml."}}
