irs though (CWD of test = crate root? cargo runs integration tests with cwd = package root). Bin tests spawn with .current_dir(tempdir) → routing.toml wouldn't be found... unless test spawns bin with current_dir = crate root or passes an env. Hmm.\\n\\nOptions: run_bin test spawns with current_dir(temp) and needs routing.toml. I could copy routing.toml into the temp dir? But binary reads \\\"routing.toml\\\" from cwd. If main resolves via discover_root() (git rev-parse), temp dir isn't a git repo → error. \\n\\nSimplest robust: main reads `routing.toml` from the current directory, falling back to CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR. In the bin test, spawn the binary with current_dir = temp dir, and first copy routing.toml from CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR into temp. That's hermetic. OK.\\n```\\n\\nActually also `resolve_repo` resolves relative repo paths against evallerina root — in dry-run, proposals just carry repo path strings; no resolution needed in dry-run? propose() just takes repo_map values as-is. to_jsonl includes repo path. Fine.\\n\\nFor `--file` path (not in tests, but wired): file_proposals needs repos to exist; main passes routing::run_bd as runner. Fine.\\n\\nWriting jsonl: next to report path → parent dir of path: `Path::new(path).parent()` — if empty use \\\".\\\". \\n\\nMain flow:\\n\\n```rust\\nif route {\\n    let root = ...; // for nothing? propose doesn't need root\\n    let content = read routing.toml (cwd, fallback manifest dir)\\n    let repo_map = evallerina::routing::parse_routing_toml(&content)?;\\n    let mut run = evallerina::routing::run_bd;\\n    let proposals = evallerina::report::attach_routing(&mut dashboard, &rows, &configured, &repo_map, file, &mut run)?;\\n    let jsonl = evallerina::routing::to_jsonl(&proposals);\\n    let out_path = report_path.parent().unwrap_or(Path::new(\\\".\\\")).join(\\\"proposed-tickets.jsonl\\\");\\n    std::fs::write(&out_path, jsonl).map_err(...)?;\\n}\\n```\\n\\nWhere should the routing.toml reading + writing jsonl live — main.rs per brief (\\\"write proposed-tickets.jsonl next to the report when routing ran\\\" listed under src/report.rs responsibilities... Brief says report.rs: \\\"call routing::propose after aggregation when --route; attach routed summary to the report JSON; write proposed-tickets.jsonl next to the report when routing ran\\\". So report.rs should do the writing too. So put a higher-level function in report.rs:\\n\\n```rust\\npub fn route_report(\\n    dashboard: &mut serde_json::Value,\\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\\n    configured_models: &[String],\\n    report_path: &Path,\\n    file_authorized: bool,\\n    run_bd: &mut BdRunner,\\n) -> Result<Vec<ProposalRow>, String>\\n```\\n\\nThis parses routing.toml (path resolution: current dir then manifest dir), attaches summary, writes jsonl. But library code writing files... acceptable given brief. But routing.toml location from library: use std::env::current_dir, fallback env!(\\\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\\\"). Library binary tests spawn bin in temp cwd with a copied routing.toml → works. Integration tests calling route_report directly would read routing.toml from crate root cwd (cargo test cwd = package root) → routing.toml present → works, but tests then write jsonl into... report_path parent — tests pass a temp path. OK.\\n\\nHmm, but tests calling attach_routing directly avoid fs. I'll split:\\n\\n- `attach_routing(dashboard, rows, configured, repo_map, file_authorized, run_bd) -> Result<Vec<ProposalRow>, String>` — pure computation.\\n- `run_routing_step(dashboard, rows, configured, report_path, file_authorized, run_bd) -> Result<Vec<ProposalRow>, String>` — loads routing.toml, calls attach_routing, writes jsonl. Used by main; bin test covers it.\\n\\nLet me now also think about `filed`/`existing` counts in dry-run: zero. Summary json:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"filed\\\": 0, \\\"existing\\\": 0, \\\"dry_run\\\": 2, \\\"skipped\\\": 1}\\n```\\n\\nTest 2 asserts dry_run > 0 and dashboard[\\\"report_version\\\"] == 1.\\n\\nTest 4: rows with a tool-fault scenario mapped but repo_map lacking the tool → skipped. In dry-run propose: unmapped tool → decision skipped, reason unmapped_tool. Summary skipped count = number of proposal rows skipped. Note proposals only exist above threshold. So fabricate 3 models × tool fault, repo_map without \\\"wai\\\" → one skipped proposal.\\n\\nTest \\\"absent rows never routed\\\": rows containing only absent kind → proposals empty, routed summary all zeros; assert dry_run==0, skipped==0, proposals.is_empty(). Note: absent rows lack tool/checks etc — aggregate_rows handles kind absent by counting coverage; propose also skips them. But rows array passed to propose — the absent row has no \\\"scenario\\\" field... in my test I'll include scenario in the absent row (the real absent record has scenario, model, repetition). propose skips before touching scenario. Good.\\n\\nAlso dashboard report_version: aggregate_rows sets report_version from rows; with absent-only rows... report_versions set is empty → defaults to 1. Good.\\n\\nBut careful: absent-only rows into aggregate_rows — coverage.absent incremented; fine.\\n\\nNow the bin tests. Use std::process::Command with env!(\\\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_evallerina\\\"). Check the bin name in Cargo.toml.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-10e4002b-448f-4db7-ab86-f8794f2c61c8","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cat Cargo.toml; echo ---; sed -n 1,60p tests/routing.rs; echo ---; grep -n \"pub mod\\|pub use\" src/lib.rs","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":6563,"output":2070,"cacheRead":26880,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":2016,"totalTokens":35513,"cost":{"input":0.00098445,"output":0.001035,"cacheRead":0.0008064,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00282585}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792429944284,"responseId":"gen-1792429944-8nh5rL9Z0vVpIPQdpaJb","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-10e4002b-448f-4db7-ab86-f8794f2c61c8","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[package]\nname = \"evallerina\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\ndescription = \"Eval battery for the dulce-de-leche tool family: do LLM agents actually use the suite's AIX output channels?\"\nlicense = \"Apache-2.0\"\nrepository = \"https://github.com/charly-vibes/evallerina\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\n\n[lib]\nname = \"evallerina\"\n\n[[bin]]\nname = \"evallerina\"\npath = \"src/main.rs\"\n\n[dependencies]\ngenesis-vibes = { git = \"https://github.com/charly-vibes/genesis\", tag = \"v0.12.3\" }\nclap = { version = \"4\", features = [\"derive\", \"env\"] }\nserde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_json = \"1\"\ntoml = \"0.8\"\nregex = \"1\"\nthiserror = \"2\"\nureq = { version = \"2\", default-features = false, features = [\"tls\", \"json\"] }\n---\n//! Purpose: integration tests for the dry-run fault routing module\n//! (evallerina-l8w, openspec add-fault-ticket-routing Phase 1).\n//! Responsibilities: pin the report.rs threshold semantics (min(3,\n//! |configured registry|) distinct models per fault key), agent-fault\n//! exclusion, unmapped-tool skip, scenario-recorded-tool repo keying,\n//! worktree-safe routing.toml path resolution, and the full\n//! proposed-tickets.jsonl row schema.\n//! Rationale: routing proposals are cross-repo actions in potentia —\n//! every decision branch (dry_run / skipped) and every schema field is\n//! machine-checked here so the CI artifact is reviewable without\n//! reading code.\n\nuse evallerina::routing;\nuse serde_json::json;\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\nuse std::sync::{Mutex, OnceLock};\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Isolation fixtures: ALL bd operations in these tests run inside a\n// per-test temp dir created under std::env::temp_dir(). The trackers of\n// evallerina and every family repo (wai/genesis/espectacular/dont) are\n// NEVER touched. bd search-style dedup always pins --status open.\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n/// Serialize per-test fixture dirs even under `cargo test` parallelism.\nfn fixture_counter() -> u64 {\n    static COUNTER: OnceLock<Mutex<u64>> = OnceLock::new();\n    let mut c = COUNTER.get_or_init(|| Mutex::new(0)).lock().unwrap();\n    *c += 1;\n    *c\n}\n\n/// An isolated temp sandbox. Deleted on drop.\nstruct Sandbox {\n    path: PathBuf,\n}\n\nimpl Sandbox {\n    /// Fresh unique dir under std::env::temp_dir().\n    fn fresh(tag: &str) -> Self {\n        let path = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(\n            \"evallerina-routing-{}-{}-{}\",\n            tag,\n            std::process::id(),\n            fixture_counter()\n                + std::time::SystemTime::now()\n                    .duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH)\n                    .unwrap()\n                    .as_nanos() as u64,\n        ));\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(&path).expect(\"create sandbox dir\");\n        Sandbox { path }\n    }\n\n    /// A sandbox with beads initialized (`bd init` inside the sandbox).\n    fn with_beads(tag: &str) -> Self {\n        let sb = Sandbox::fresh(tag);\n        routing::run_bd(&sb.path, &[\"init\"]).expect(\"bd init in sandbox\");\n        sb\n    }\n---\n14:pub mod ablation;\n15:pub mod envelope;\n16:pub mod live;\n17:pub mod recorded;\n18:pub mod registry;\n19:pub mod report;\n20:pub mod routing;\n21:pub mod scenario;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792430021491}]}
