{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":9464,"output":3455,"cacheRead":26880,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3376,"totalTokens":39799,"cost":{"input":0.0014196,"output":0.0017274999999999999,"cacheRead":0.0008064,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0039534999999999995}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I have full picture. Let me follow TDD. Also check the registry REGISTRY ids (models used in tests via models(n)).\n\nTest plan for tests/report_aggregation.rs additions (new section \"routing wiring (evallerina-o3j)\"):\n\n1. `file_without_route_is_an_error` — validate_route_flags(false, true) err; combos ok.\n2. `route_dry_run_attaches_routed_summary` — rows: 3 models tool_fault on \"wai-hint-adherence-typo\", repo_map wai→../wai. attach_routing → dashboard[\"routed\"] present with dry_run=1, filed=0, existing=0, skipped=0; report_version still 1; dashboard_version unchanged; no \"score\".\n3. `report_without_route_has_no_routed_field` — bin test: run binary without --route → stdout JSON has no routed; no proposed-tickets.jsonl. (Library-level: aggregate_rows output has no routed — trivially true; the bin test is the real check.)\n4. `unmapped_tool_counts_skipped_and_report_succeeds` — same rows, empty repo_map → Ok, routed.skipped == 1, dry_run == 0.\n5. `absent_rows_never_routed` — rows = [absent record] with --route → all zeros, proposals empty.\n6. bin test `route_dry_run_writes_proposed_tickets_jsonl` — temp dir, copy routing.toml from CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR, write rows.jsonl (3 models tool fault, scenario wai-hint-adherence-typo, tool \"wai\"... wait — propose keys repo on scenario-recorded tool, which via scenario_tool_of(\"wai-hint-adherence-typo\") = \"wai\". Row tool field is provenance only. Good.) Run `evallerina report rows.jsonl --route` → stdout has routed.dry_run == 1, proposed-tickets.jsonl exists with the token line.\n\nWait — configured models in main come from registry ordered_ids(); registry has ≥3? Check registry REGISTRY length. tests use REGISTRY.iter().take(3). Fine — 3 distinct real model ids.\n\nCareful with scenario_tool_of: routing tests used \"wai-hint-adherence-typo\" → wai. But what about \"wai-doc-drift-stale-agents-md\"? starts with \"wai-\" → wai. \"dont-hint-adherence-lifecycle\" → dont. Good.\n\nAlso routing threshold in propose: configured.len().min(3). Registry probably has 3-5 models.\n\nBin test spawn: Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_evallerina\")).args([\"report\", \"rows.jsonl\", \"--route\"]).current_dir(&sandbox).output(). stdout is pretty-printed JSON. Parse.\n\nOne issue: main.rs Report variant currently prints dashboard to stdout; keep. The `routed` field attached to dashboard JSON.\n\nAlso --file in main.rs: file_authorized passed to attach_routing. In bin tests we never pass --file (anti-goal for CI but local test is fine — actually brief test list doesn't require --file bin test; CLI --file wiring exists but testing it would call bd in mapped repos! Do NOT test --file bin-level. Only flag validation test.)\n\nNow GHA workflow step 5: add artifact upload of proposed-tickets.jsonl after rotation. But the rotation workflow runs `live` and tees to reports/tier2-rotation.jsonl; where does the report step run? The workflow currently doesn't run `report` at all! Brief: \"the tier-2 GHA rotation uploads the dry-run artifact\". So add a step running `cargo run --release -- report reports/tier2-rotation.jsonl --route` writing reports/proposed-tickets.jsonl, then upload both artifacts. And grep-assert no \"--file\" in workflow. Let me write:\n\n```yaml\n      - name: Aggregate + route (dry-run)\n        run: |\n          cargo run --release -- report reports/tier2-rotation.jsonl --route\n        # never --file: filing is a local, explicitly-authorized action\n```\n\nWait: does `report` write proposed-tickets.jsonl next to the report path → reports/proposed-tickets.jsonl. Good.\n\nThen:\n\n```yaml\n      - name: Upload proposed tickets (dry-run artifact)\n        if: always()\n        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\n        with:\n          name: proposed-tickets\n          path: reports/proposed-tickets.jsonl\n```\n\nNote `if: always()` — if rotation failed, tier2-rotation.jsonl still exists. But if the report step didn't run, the artifact step would fail with missing path... upload-artifact with a missing file fails unless if-no-files-found. Add `if-no-files-found: warn`. Good.\n\nNow the summary counts on proposed rows: dry_run counts mapped proposals. If the rotation had no threshold faults, proposals empty → jsonl empty file. Fine.\n\nImplementation details for report.rs:\n\n```rust\nuse crate::routing;\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\n\n/// --file without --route is a loud CLI error...\npub fn validate_route_flags(route: bool, file: bool) -> Result<(), String> {\n    if file && !route {\n        return Err(\"--file requires --route: filing proposed tickets only makes sense after the routing step ran\".into());\n    }\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n/// The scenario definition's recorded tool — the repo key for routing\n/// (routing.rs keys proposals on this, never the row's tool field).\n/// Scenario names prefix-encode the eval target by convention\n/// (`wai-*`, `dont-*`); an unknown prefix is None → loud error\n/// downstream (never a silent bucket).\npub fn scenario_tool_of(name: &str) -> Option<String> {\n    if name.starts_with(\"wai-\") {\n        Some(\"wai\".to_owned())\n    } else if name.starts_with(\"dont-\") {\n        Some(\"dont\".to_owned())\n    } else {\n        None\n    }\n}\n\npub fn attach_routing(...) -> Result<Vec<routing::ProposalRow>, String> {\n    let mut proposals = routing::propose(rows, configured_models, &scenario_tool_of, repo_map)?;\n    routing::file_proposals(&mut proposals, file_authorized, run_bd)?;\n    let (mut filed, mut existing, mut dry_run, mut skipped) = (0usize, 0, 0, 0);\n    for p in &proposals {\n        match p.decision.as_str() {\n            \"filed\" => filed += 1,\n            \"existing\" => existing += 1,\n            \"dry_run\" => dry_run += 1,\n            _ => skipped += 1,\n        }\n    }\n    dashboard[\"routed\"] = json!({\n        \"filed\": filed, \"existing\": existing, \"dry_run\": dry_run, \"skipped\": skipped,\n    });\n    Ok(proposals)\n}\n```\n\nNote dashboard is serde_json::Value object; indexing assignment `dashboard[\"routed\"] = ...` requires it to be an Object — aggregate_rows output is object, fine. But assigning to a Value via IndexMut on non-object panics; aggregate output always object. OK.\n\nfile_proposals signature: `run_bd: &mut BdRunner` where BdRunner = dyn FnMut(...). In attach_routing: `run_bd: &mut routing::BdRunner` — passing along. Note file_proposals with file_authorized=false returns Ok immediately; run_bd unused but we must still pass. Passing `run_bd: &mut BdRunner` generic lifetime fine.\n\nMain.rs:\n\n```rust\nReport {\n    path: String,\n    /// Run the fault-routing step after aggregation (dry-run by\n    /// default): attach the additive `routed` summary to the dashboard\n    /// and write proposed-tickets.jsonl next to the report.\n    #[arg(long)]\n    route: bool,\n    /// File the proposed tickets in their mapped repositories\n    /// (explicit cross-repo write authorization). Requires --route.\n    #[arg(long)]\n    file: bool,\n},\n```\n\nrun_report:\n\n```rust\nfn run_report(path: &str, route: bool, file: bool) -> Result<ExitCode, String> {\n    evallerina::report::validate_route_flags(route, file)?;\n    ... rows parse (existing) ...\n    let configured: Vec<String> = ordered_ids()...;\n    let mut dashboard = aggregate_rows(...)?;\n    if route {\n        evallerina::report::run_routing_step(\n            &mut dashboard, &rows, &configured, std::path::Path::new(path), file, &mut evallerina::routing::run_bd,\n        )?;\n    }\n    println!(...);\n    Ok(ExitCode::SUCCESS)\n}\n```\n\nrun_routing_step in report.rs:\n\n```rust\npub fn run_routing_step(\n    dashboard: &mut serde_json::Value,\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\n    configured_models: &[String],\n    report_path: &std::path::Path,\n    file_authorized: bool,\n    run_bd: &mut routing::BdRunner,\n) -> Result<Vec<routing::ProposalRow>, String> {\n    let content = std::fs::read_to_string(\"routing.toml\")\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot read routing.toml: {e}\"))?;\n    let repo_map = routing::parse_routing_toml(&content)?;\n    let proposals = attach_routing(dashboard, rows, configured_models, &repo_map, file_authorized, run_bd)?;\n    let jsonl = routing::to_jsonl(&proposals);\n    let out_path = report_path.parent().unwrap_or(std::path::Path::new(\".\")).join(\"proposed-tickets.jsonl\");\n    std::fs::write(&out_path, jsonl).map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot write {}: {e}\", out_path.display()))?;\n    Ok(proposals)\n}\n```\n\nNote: reading \"routing.toml\" from cwd. In bin tests, sandbox cwd must contain routing.toml (copy from manifest dir). In real usage (CI/local) cwd = repo root. Acceptable; document.\n\nHmm wait — `routing::run_bd` is a fn item; `&mut evallerina::routing::run_bd` coerces to &mut dyn FnMut? BdRunner = dyn FnMut(&Path, &[&str]) -> BdResult. `run_bd` fn signature matches. `&mut run_bd` — need a local binding: `let mut runner = evallerina::routing::run_bd; ... &mut runner` to coerce. Function item coerces to fn pointer then to dyn. `&mut evallerina::routing::run_bd` might coerce directly via unsized coercion? For a function item, `&mut F` → `&mut dyn FnMut` requires the function item to coerce to the trait object; unsized coercion from fn item reference... Standard pattern: define `let mut runner: routing::BdRunner = routing::run_bd;` hmm that's a binding of dyn type. Actually `fn file_proposals(..., run_bd: &mut BdRunner)`. Passing `&mut routing::run_bd` — the expression `routing::run_bd` is a fn item value; taking `&mut` gives `&mut FnDef`; coercion `&mut FnDef -> &mut dyn FnMut` works (function items implement FnMut). I believe `&mut run_bd` where run