est red-green for step 4: it likely already passes. The brief says \\\"RED: routing failures (unmapped tool) → skipped counted\\\". propose() already handles unmapped. The wiring (count skipped in summary) happens in step 2's attach_routing. So step 4's test verifies existing behavior. I'll note in the report that steps 3-4 tests were contract-pinning and green on first run (behavior inherited from step 2 + routing.rs); that's fine.\\n\\nAlternatively sequence differently: make step 2 only implement dry_run counting... No, keep it simple and honest in the report.\\n\\nLet's start. First write step 1 test.\\n\\nTest file location: tests/report_aggregation.rs. Add section at end.\\n\\n```rust\\n// ── CLI routing wiring (evallerina-o3j) ─────────────────────────────────────\\n\\n/// `--file` without `--route` is a loud error: filing is a cross-repo\\n/// write that only makes sense after the routing step ran.\\n#[test]\\nfn file_without_route_is_an_error() {\\n    assert!(evallerina::report::validate_route_flags(false, true).is_err());\\n    assert!(evallerina::report::validate_route_flags(true, true).is_ok());\\n    assert!(evallerina::report::validate_route_flags(true, false).is_ok());\\n    assert!(evallerina::report::validate_route_flags(false, false).is_ok());\\n}\\n```\\n\\nRun: fails (no function). Then implement + main flags. Note: if I add clap flags to main.rs in the same commit but never use route/file... main will call validate_route_flags in run_report in commit 1? run_report signature change: run_report(&path, route, file) calling validate_route_flags first. Then commit 2 wires route. Actually commit 1 could wire both flags and validation; commit 2 wires routing execution. Fine.\\n\\nDead code warnings: route/file params used. OK.\\n\\nAlso need `mut dashboard` binding in run_report for commit 2.\\n\\nLet me now check registry to know ordered_ids size.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the full picture. Let me chec