ashboard: &mut serde_json::Value,\\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\\n    configured_models: &[String],\\n    repo_map: &BTreeMap<String, String>,\\n    file_authorized: bool,\\n    run_bd: &mut BdRunner,\\n) -> Result<serde_json::Value, String>\\n```\\n\\nHmm, but tests in tests/report_aggregation.rs need to test: routed field present after --route dry-run; report_version still 1; --file without --route is an error (CLI level — that's main.rs, testable via assert on CLI parsing? It's a runtime check in main, hard to test from integration test unless the check is in report.rs). Let me put the validation in report.rs: a function that errors if file_authorized && !route. Actually cleaner: in main.rs clap, `--file` requires `--route` — clap supports `requires` but that auto-enables. We want --file without --route → error. clap's `requires_ifs`/conflicts... Actually we want: `--file` errors unless `--route`. In clap, `#[arg(long, requires = \\\"route\\\")]` makes --route required when --file present — that gives error \\\"the following required arguments were not provided: --route\\\". That's exactly \\\"--file requires --route; error otherwise\\\". And it's testable via `Cli::try_parse`. But Cli is in main.rs (binary), not accessible from integration tests. Tests/report_aggregation.rs is an integration test against the lib. So the CLI flag test can't reach the binary's Cli struct.\\n\\nOptions: put the validation in report.rs as a function that main calls, e.g.:\\n\\n```rust\\npub fn validate_route_flags(route: bool, file: bool) -> Result<(), String> {\\n    if file && !route {\\n        return Err(\\\"--file requires --route\\\".into());\\n    }\\n    Ok(())\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThen test: validate_route_flags(false, true).is_err(). And main.rs uses clap requires too? Keep both? Simplest: do the check in report.rs (tested) and in main.rs Report variant run_report takes (path, route, file) and errors. Actually I'll have main.rs parse flags and call report.rs functions; the c