hes summary, writes jsonl. But library code writing files... acceptable given brief. But routing.toml location from library: use std::env::current_dir, fallback env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\"). Library binary tests spawn bin in temp cwd with a copied routing.toml → works. Integration tests calling route_report directly would read routing.toml from crate root cwd (cargo test cwd = package root) → routing.toml present → works, but tests then write jsonl into... report_path parent — tests pass a temp path. OK.\n\nHmm, but tests calling attach_routing directly avoid fs. I'll split:\n\n- `attach_routing(dashboard, rows, configured, repo_map, file_authorized, run_bd) -> Result<Vec<ProposalRow>, String>` — pure computation.\n- `run_routing_step(dashboard, rows, configured, report_path, file_authorized, run_bd) -> Result<Vec<ProposalRow>, String>` — loads routing.toml, calls attach_routing, writes jsonl. Used by main; bin test covers it.\n\nLet me now also think about `filed`/`existing` counts in dry-run: zero. Summary json:\n\n```json\n{\"filed\": 0, \"existing\": 0, \"dry_run\": 2, \"skipped\": 1}\n```\n\nTest 2 asserts dry_run > 0 and dashboard[\"report_version\"] == 1.\n\nTest 4: rows with a tool-fault scenario mapped but repo_map lacking the tool → skipped. In dry-run propose: unmapped tool → decision skipped, reason unmapped_tool. Summary skipped count = number of proposal rows skipped. Note proposals only exist above threshold. So fabricate 3 models × tool fault, repo_map without \"wai\" → one skipped proposal.\n\nTest \"absent rows never routed\": rows containing only absent kind → proposals empty, routed summary all zeros; assert dry_run==0, skipped==0, proposals.is_empty(). Note: absent rows lack tool/checks etc — aggregate_rows handles kind absent by counting coverage; propose also skips them. But rows array passed to propose — the absent row has no \"scenario\" field... in my test I'll include scenario in the absent row (the real absent record has scenario, model, 